## 3. Architecture Decisions

### One Builder, One Runtime, Multiple Presentation Contexts

The platform will continue to use:

- one Builder
- one published Performance Sheet model
- one Assignment model
- one Runtime execution engine

Different user experiences may present the same underlying execution data.

Member Workspace is therefore a presentation, navigation, and workflow layer over Runtime.

It is not a second performance engine.

### Member Workspace / Runtime Relationship

The Member Workspace will sit on top of the existing Runtime execution architecture.

The intended relationship is:

Builder Definition
↓
Published Performance Sheet
↓
Assignment
↓
Performance Instance
↓
Runtime Execution
↓
Member Workspace

The Member Workspace may provide:

- current performance view
- assigned Performance Sheet
- Objectives
- Key Results
- current KPI/progress values
- comments
- status
- completion/progress context
- relevant employee actions

These capabilities must be sourced from Runtime and related domain services.

### No Member-Specific Performance Model

Member Workspace must not create member-specific copies of:

- Objectives
- Key Results
- Initiatives
- Performance Sheets
- KPI calculations
- Assignments
- Performance Instances

Reusable definitions remain Builder-owned.

Period-specific execution state remains Runtime-owned.

### Monthly Cadence Remains a Product Rule

The platform continues to treat monthly performance cadence as product behavior.

Member Workspace should not introduce an administrator-managed arbitrary Reporting Period entity.

Runtime should continue resolving the applicable execution context from the existing period architecture.

### Current Scoring Remains Runtime Logic

The current Runtime scoring utility remains intentionally simple:

current value / target × 100

with the current 0–100 scoring behavior.

This does not become member-specific logic.

The generalized KPI Calculation Engine and weighted aggregation remain future platform capabilities.

### Production Security Remains Separate

The current organization query context is not authorization.

Member Workspace implementation must not imply production authorization before the authentication and tenant-security milestones are completed.

Future member access must be enforced using authenticated identity and server-side authorization.

