## 9. Technical Debt / Deferred Work

### Production Authentication

Authentication is not yet the production security boundary for Member Workspace.

Future implementation must connect member identity to authenticated platform identity.

### Production Tenant Authorization

Organization context must eventually be derived and validated from authenticated membership rather than trusted from a client-supplied organization identifier.

### PostgreSQL Row Level Security

RLS remains outstanding.

Future RLS policies must enforce tenant isolation at the database layer where appropriate.

### Runtime Security

Runtime currently provides the execution architecture but production access control remains a separate security milestone.

Member Workspace must not bypass Runtime security boundaries.

### Assignment Subject Validation

Assignment subject validation remains deferred.

Future hardening should ensure that an Assignment can only target valid subjects within the appropriate organization and subject type.

### Performance Instance Relationship Integrity

The relationship between Assignment, Performance Sheet version, Performance Instance, subject, and period requires continued hardening.

Member Workspace should consume this relationship rather than reconstruct it.

### Historical KPI Updates

Historical KPI update storage remains future work.

Member Workspace should not invent a separate historical KPI storage model.

### Generalized KPI Calculation Engine

The current scoring utility remains intentionally small.

A generalized KPI Calculation Engine remains future platform work.

### Weighted Aggregation

Formal weighted aggregation across Key Results, Objectives, and Performance Instances remains future work.

### Historical Performance Reporting

Historical reporting remains future work and should eventually be built from persisted Runtime history rather than member-specific reporting copies.

